Three views (0.7, native/quadviews/dcsvr_threeviews.h explains the pass): the periphery views' depth is always wanted
from the engine (DcsVr_QuadViewsDepthWanted bits 0 and 1, besides Far depth's 2 and 3); only an engine that renders
the right periphery as its outer strip plus the cockpit (DcsQvCull [Views] ThreeViews) pushes them, the right one
flagged DCSVR_DEPTH_THREE_VIEWS (dcsvr_depth_export.h v1.2). In such a frame the right eye's periphery source is
replaced, before periphery stability, contrast and the composition, by a layer-owned image: DCS's own pixels in the
strip and on the cockpit, the left periphery reprojected with its depth everywhere else. Without those pushes nothing
changes. The depth import's device is now set whether Far depth is on or not.

